# Sentient gateway — example env vars for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored) and adjust as needed:
#     cp gateway/.env.example gateway/.env
#
# Bun auto-loads `.env` from the current working directory at startup,
# so `bun run --cwd gateway dev` will pick up `gateway/.env` automatically.
#
# ⚠️  Production uses a different mechanism — NEVER deploy these values.
#     In prod, inject PASETO_SECRET_KEY and API keys via your deployment
#     system (Docker env, Kubernetes secret, systemd EnvironmentFile, etc.)
#     and keep `.env` out of production images.

# ─── Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Web auth is currently bypassed — the gateway accepts every WebSocket
# connection on the LAN until a proper role-based login flow is added.
# Service-to-service auth (gateway <-> capability services) is managed by
# sentient-auth (see sentient-auth/README.md). Tokens live in
# ~/.sentient/auth/tokens/<service>.yaml.

# ─── Static file serving (Phase 3 web client) ───────────────────────────────
#
# Absolute path to the built Preact client. Leave unset to disable static
# serving (gateway only exposes /ws and /health). Required to open the app
# in a browser at http://localhost:3000.
WEB_DIST_DIR=/Users/kevinye/Development/sentient/web/dist

# ─── Provider API keys (optional for local dev) ─────────────────────────────
#
# Without these, the gateway still authenticates and accepts text input, but
# has no LLM to reply with — you'll get `provider_error: LLM provider not
# configured` back in the chat.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# CHAT_MODEL=anthropic/claude-3-haiku

# Override to point at any OpenAI-compatible endpoint — e.g., a local
# model server (Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, llama.cpp). Leave unset for
# hosted OpenRouter.
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# ─── Server binding ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GATEWAY_PORT=3000
# GATEWAY_HOST=0.0.0.0
